Anthony, 2026-10-22, on the Riemann-map rung's question ("Go with your recommendations for questions 1 through 3").

MEASURED: design 5cdc6110fcaa5ad5 had to join RH and Robin's inequality with DUPLICATES. detect_defects then proposed MERGING them (suggested_fix_type: merge), which would destroy the map; the owner acknowledged both suggestions as wrong. The seven equivalence theorems sat isolated, because two inference steps would form a cycle, and a step concluding RH would make RH read conditional.

WHAT IT ASKS: a relation between two statements, backed by a cited or proven biconditional, that:
(1) reads as "equivalent", never "duplicate", and is never offered for merge;
(2) leaves each side's own reading unchanged: an open conjecture stays open;
(3) shows in a what-if that refuting or establishing one side reaches the other;
(4) gives the speculative-link circularity check (dec:idea-speculate-the-bridge-that-would-close-a-gap-then-test-it) what it needs, so a proposed bridge equivalent to the gap is flagged mechanically, not by the agent's judgment alone.

Built in the queued reflow2 PR "proofs and arguments read right". Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Xbw6PG9mXJiU2Sb421fnq
